  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Use the division algorithm to divide $P(x)$ by $D(x)$. Express each result in the form $P(x)=D(x)Q(x)+R(x)$, where either $R(x)=0$ or the degree of $R(x)$ is less than the degree of $D(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^2+8x+6$, $D(x)=x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x+2)(x+6)-6$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms successively:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2\\div x&=x\\\\(x^2+8x+6)-x(x+2)&=6x+6\\\\6x\\div x&=6\\\\(6x+6)-6(x+2)&=-6\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x+6$ and $R(x)=-6$.\n$$P(x)=(x+2)(x+6)-6.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3-6x^2-12x+30$, $D(x)=x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x+6)(x^2-12x+60)-330$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms successively:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3\\div x&=x^2\\\\(x^3-6x^2-12x+30)-x^2(x+6)&=-12x^2-12x+30\\\\-12x^2\\div x&=-12x\\\\(-12x^2-12x+30)-(-12x)(x+6)&=60x+30\\\\60x\\div x&=60\\\\(60x+30)-60(x+6)&=-330\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x^2-12x+60$ and $R(x)=-330$.\n$$P(x)=(x+6)(x^2-12x+60)-330.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=5x^3-7x^2-1$, $D(x)=x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x-1)(5x^2-2x-2)-3$",
          "worked": "Write the missing $x$ term as $0x$ and divide the leading terms successively:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=5x^3-7x^2+0x-1\\\\5x^3\\div x&=5x^2\\\\(5x^3-7x^2+0x-1)-5x^2(x-1)&=-2x^2+0x-1\\\\-2x^2\\div x&=-2x\\\\(-2x^2+0x-1)-(-2x)(x-1)&=-2x-1\\\\-2x\\div x&=-2\\\\(-2x-1)-(-2)(x-1)&=-3\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=5x^2-2x-2$ and $R(x)=-3$.\n$$P(x)=(x-1)(5x^2-2x-2)-3.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
